Backport of magento/magento2 AC-17650 (merge 3a6b9667113, 2026-08-28) together with its prerequisite ACP2E-4989 (327d5bfa12d) to Magento 2.4.9 (framework 103.0.9).
Fixes the Symfony cache Redis tag index leak (cache:id_tags:* / cache:tags:* / cache:all_ids never pruned), L2 flush/clean, lifetime and compression handling.
Built on top of allow-to-use-own-cache-dir.patch (upstream now returns absolute cache_dir as-is), so it has to be applied after it.
Test files and dev/ changes are left out.
Also contains the fork fixes of magento/magento2@19640e886e and the database-scoped persistent_id of @4d6f3a65a5 (AC-17867), so parallel indexers (MAGE_INDEXER_THREADS_COUNT > 1) no longer share the parent's Redis socket. This replaces the former optional 249-fix-parallel-indexer-shared-redis-connection.patch.
Also contains the SymfonyL2Cache::save() fix of magento/magento2@0be8c3325ea (AC-17867): a tagged save of data that L2 already holds removes the remote entry and saves it again, so a changed tag set and lifetime reach Redis instead of being skipped as a redundant write.
Also contains the fix for magento/magento2#41529 from PR #41719 (open upstream): the pipelined tag index prune, used when Redis refuses EVAL (ACL without scripts, RedisCluster), keeps the index of ids whose data key still exists, as the atomic Lua prune does.
Also resets the symfony_l2 regeneration-lock state (cached lock adapter, signature, held locks) in a forked child, so the lock commands of parallel indexers do not run over the parent's Redis connection (the same reply mix-up as above; upstream 2.4-develop still caches the lock adapter across forks).

